Subject: [PATCH] ldpd: terminate local host FECs like connected routes

Zebra reports interface host addresses as ZEBRA_ROUTE_LOCAL. Without the
connected flag their interface-only nexthops are skipped, so LDP never
advertises an egress binding for the /32 or /128. OSPFv3 point-to-point
host advertisements expose the missing binding along an otherwise working
LSP. Use the existing connected-route label allocation and withdrawal path.

--- a/ldpd/ldp_zebra.c
+++ b/ldpd/ldp_zebra.c
@@ -521,6 +521,7 @@
 
 	switch (api.type) {
 	case ZEBRA_ROUTE_CONNECT:
+	case ZEBRA_ROUTE_LOCAL:
 		SET_FLAG(kr.flags, F_CONNECTED);
 		break;
 	case ZEBRA_ROUTE_BGP:
